  "notes": "ゆっくりと is an adverb meaning 'slowly' or 'at ease,' describing actions done without haste.\n\nFORM:\nゆっくりと and ゆっくり are interchangeable. The と particle adds slight emphasis or formality.\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Slowly (pace/speed): ゆっくりと{歩|ある}く (walk slowly)\n2. At ease/leisurely (manner): ゆっくりと{過|す}ごす (spend time leisurely)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ゆっくり{休|やす}んでください: Please rest well\n- ゆっくり{話|はな}してください: Please speak slowly\n- ゆっくりしていってください: Please take your time / stay and relax\n- ゆっくりでいいですよ: Take your time, no rush\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {早|はや}く: quickly, fast\n- {急|いそ}いで: in a hurry\n\nSIMILAR:\n- のんびり: leisurely, carefree\n- ゆったり: spaciously, relaxedly",
